# Measured with native LAMMPS: engine vs native (b332f28, /home/roy/.local/bin/lmp, PKG REPLICA, MPI, 2 partitions) per partition: thermo max err 3.4e-11 (relative), per-atom max 6.1e-11 (18 atoms, 6 waters, npt on the mixed pressure, 200 steps, about 1.2-1.5 s engine incl. node start).
# oracle: w194alc_water — fix alchemy on 2 partitions, a water-like system (6 water molecules, bonds and angles from a data file) with fix npt on the mixed pressure (fix_modify press pressure with compute pressure/alchemy); the partitions differ in the charges of the first two molecules (the example in.twowater changes the topology too, which the engine does not do yet)
# oracle-partitions: 2
# oracle-inputs: w194alc_water.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10
variable name world twowater twoions
units real
atom_style full
atom_modify map array
boundary p p p
read_data w194alc_water.data
pair_style lj/cut/coul/cut 6.0
pair_coeff 1 1 0.1553 3.166
pair_coeff 1 2 0.0 1.0
pair_coeff 2 2 0.0 1.0
bond_style harmonic
bond_coeff 1 1000.0 1.0
angle_style harmonic
angle_coeff 1 100.0 109.47
group transform id 1:6
if "${name} == twoions" then "set atom 1 charge -1.1354" "set atom 2 charge 0.1354" "set atom 3 charge 0.56775" "set atom 4 charge -0.70305" "set atom 5*6 charge 0.56775"
velocity all create 300.0 5463576
timestep 0.2
if "${name} == twowater" then "variable ramp equal ramp(1.0,0.0)" else "variable ramp equal ramp(0.0,1.0)"
fix integrate all npt temp 300 300 1.0 iso 1.0 1.0 10.0
fix transform all alchemy v_ramp
compute pressure all pressure/alchemy transform
fix_modify integrate press pressure
thermo_style custom step temp press etotal density pe ke f_transform f_transform[3]
thermo_modify press pressure
thermo_modify format float %.15g
thermo 20
run 200
